        <h1 class="post-detail__title">Community Counts: Teton Arts</h1>

        <div class="post-detail__featured-image">
          <img src="/assets/images/news/50080.webp" alt="Community Counts: Teton Arts" loading="lazy">
        </div>

        <div class="post-detail__content">
          <p>Kurt Vonnegut said it best when he said, “Practicing an art, no matter how well or badly, is a way to make your soul grow, for heaven’s sake&#8230;Do it as well as you possibly can.&nbsp;&nbsp;You will get an enormous reward.&nbsp;&nbsp;You will have created something.”</p>

<p>Embracing creative experiences as a universal tool to improve quality of life, <a href="https://www.tetonarts.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">Teton Arts</a> has set out to grow our program offerings to engage as many people as we can.&nbsp;&nbsp;Our weekly adult classes not only offer the opportunity to practice making pottery or painting but create a space for people to gather and socialize, strengthening our community through these creative experiences.</p>

<p>To further foster community, Teton Arts hosts free potlucks followed by art activities.&nbsp;&nbsp;These bi-weekly potlucks bring community members together to catch up or meet each other for the first time.&nbsp;&nbsp;Families are encouraged to come together and nourish their bodies and then to also exercise their imagination as they create!&nbsp;&nbsp;Our Bi-Annual open houses are a fun time when our neighbors can come together and enjoy the community studio.&nbsp;&nbsp;Family-friendly art activities and events like scavenger hunts or collaborative community art projects give everyone an opportunity to work together and create.</p>

<p>We engage children in art through field trips with school groups, after-school art programs, and summer camps.&nbsp;&nbsp;Field trips are a great way for teachers to use Teton Arts as a resource to reinforce classroom education adding more creative outlets for their young learners.&nbsp;&nbsp;Our after-school programs provide inspiring childcare at our elementary schools making it easy and convenient for working families.&nbsp;&nbsp;Summer camp has been a growing program where we have designed an interactive and fun environment for kids to create and grow their imaginations throughout the summer.&nbsp;&nbsp;Our summer programs are choice-based allowing kids to determine the activities and art mediums they work with every day.&nbsp;&nbsp;Playing outside, especially during group-building games, teaches kids key aspects of community, collaboration, and teamwork as they learn to work together.&nbsp;&nbsp;Creating an environment where kids feel safe exploring their imaginations and practicing their creativity allows them to grow in&nbsp;incredibly impactful ways.</p>

<p>&nbsp;To ensure that every family in our valley has access to these programs, we offer sliding scale scholarships.&nbsp;&nbsp;Families are invited to apply for scholarships,&nbsp;paying what they can to attend our programs.&nbsp;&nbsp;To this day we are proud to share that we have never turned away a scholarship applicant.&nbsp;&nbsp;Through scholarships, work-trade, and free community potlucks we aim to make opportunities for everyone in Teton Valley to join us and create!</p>

